    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change\n\nAdded `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode` \u2014 to the owner API response.\n\n**Three small, cohesive edits:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared a new read-only `checkDigit` property (int32, 0\u20139) on the owner schema, which regenerates the `checkDigit` field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`util/Luhn.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny self-contained utility with a single static `checkDigit(String)` method that sums the string's digits with Luhn doubling and returns `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` line delegating to `Luhn.checkDigit(...)`, guarding null `customerCode`.\n\n## Structural-impact notes\n\nI kept the cost low by putting the logic in a **brand-new class** (`Luhn`) whose `WMC_other` is 0 \u2014 so its complexity carries no surrounding-context penalty. The only edit to an existing class is a single declarative mapping annotation on `OwnerMapper` (no method bodies grown, matching the existing `identityKey`/`membershipNumber` idiom). This mirrors the established pattern of small util classes (`IdentityKeys`, `Localities`, `E164`) plus expression-based mappings.\n\n## Tests\n\n`mvn test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes (recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit`).",
